 ## Subtopics
 
 ### Volume Rendering with MTD
-This variant integrates the MTD representation with a specific volume rendering pipeline. It models density and appearance fields separately using two MTD representations. Density $\sigma_i$ is the softplus of the sum of feature vectors at all levels. Color composition weights $w_i$ are computed based on densities and sampling intervals $\Delta_i$. To reduce computational cost, colors are only computed for sampled points where $w_i$ exceeds a predefined threshold. The final color is a weighted sum of predicted colors. The specular color is predicted by a directional MLP fed with an encoded feature vector $g$ and a bottleneck feature $b$, while diffuse color and specular weight are predicted by the spatial MLP. The spatial MLP has 3 layers and the directional MLP has 6 layers [S1].
